# Rust
**/target/

# .NET
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/TestResults/
# CI (hyper-pack-nuget.yml) arranges and packs these per-RID at pack time; regenerable
# locally via `cargo cdylib` (the csproj's runtimes/**/native/* wildcard item).
csharp/HyperTabular/runtimes/
# The same for the static libraries a Native AOT publish links in: staged by the forge's
# static-libs/build-static-libs.sh at test and pack time, never committed.
csharp/HyperTabular/staticlibs/

# Gradle / Java
**/.gradle/
**/build/
# CI (hyper-publish-maven.yml) bundles all platforms' natives here at publish time; the
# local dev loop stages into build/generated-resources instead (already covered by
# **/build/ above), so anything here is regenerable via `cargo cdylib`.
java/src/main/resources/native/
# csharp/HyperTabular/build/ is NuGet's real, tracked build/{PackageId}.targets packaging
# convention (auto-imported into every consumer for the browser-wasm NativeFileReference and
# EmccExportedFunction wiring — see HyperTabular.csproj), not a build output. It collides with
# **/build/ above, which would otherwise silently swallow it: the file would sit on disk,
# pack correctly in a local `dotnet pack`, and simply never exist in CI. Each directory level
# needs its own negation — git won't descend into an excluded directory to find a deeper
# !file re-inclusion — and gitignore rules apply in file order, so this must come after the
# rule it un-ignores. HyperUuid carries the same block for the same reason.
!csharp/HyperTabular/build/
!csharp/HyperTabular/build/net10.0/
!csharp/HyperTabular/build/net10.0/HyperTabular.targets

# Python
**/__pycache__/
**/*.egg-info/
**/.venv/
**/dist/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
# The staged PyO3 extension for local dev/test — nested at hypertabular._native (the maturin
# module-name), built from the core crate's python feature. Its file name varies with the
# Python version and platform (_native.abi3.so, _native.abi3t-darwin.so,
# _native.cpython-314t-<platform>.so and more), so these match every compiled spelling and
# nothing else: _native.pyi beside them is the tracked type stub.
python/src/hypertabular/_native*.so
python/src/hypertabular/_native*.pyd

# Swift
# The core in the artifact bundle and the XCFramework is build output: CI and
# .github/scripts/local-core.sh write it, and consumers get it from the release's assets (the
# root Package.swift). Only the bundle's include/ (header and module map) is source.
**/.build/
swift/HyperTabularCore.artifactbundle/*
!swift/HyperTabularCore.artifactbundle/include/
swift/HyperTabularCoreApple.xcframework/

# Ruby
# CI places each leg's native lib here for `bundle exec rspec` at build-native time, and
# rubygems-publish stages all eight into the universal gem at gem-build time (the platform
# gems carry none); regenerable locally via `cargo cdylib`.
ruby/lib/hypertabular/native/*/
ruby/Gemfile.lock
ruby/pkg/
ruby/.yardoc/
# The wasm32-wasip1 archives `rake wasm:gem` packs (and their .gz), staged from CI's
# ruby-wasm-<minor> artifacts by release.yml, or by hand; never committed.
ruby/ext/hypertabular_native/*/
# rbwasm's interpreter build and its output, from running ruby/wasm-smoke locally.
ruby/wasm-smoke/Gemfile.lock
ruby/wasm-smoke/build/
ruby/wasm-smoke/rubies/
ruby/wasm-smoke/*.wasm
# Staged Magnus extension for local dev/test (built from the core crate's ruby feature;
# precompiled platform gems carry the real artifact).
ruby/lib/hypertabular_native.so
ruby/lib/hypertabular_native.bundle
# The per-ABI staging the fat platform gem is packed from (lib/hypertabular/<minor>/), written
# by release.yml from CI artifacts. Same story as the flat pair above: build output, never
# committed. Scoped to the extension filename rather than the whole directory so it can't
# swallow a real lib/hypertabular/*.rb source file if a minor-version-shaped one ever appears.
ruby/lib/hypertabular/*/hypertabular_native.so
ruby/lib/hypertabular/*/hypertabular_native.bundle

# PHP
php/vendor/
php/composer.lock
php/.phpunit.result.cache
# The root composer.json is the PIE package's metadata, not a project anyone installs from
# the repo root, but a stray local `composer install` there shouldn't get committed either.
/vendor/
/composer.lock
php/.phpunit.result.cache
# Root-level composer.json exists only for Packagist (see php/README.md's Install section) —
# nothing actually runs `composer install` from the repo root except a consumer's own build,
# but a stray local one shouldn't get committed either.
/vendor/
/composer.lock

# Node: the TypeScript binding and ruby/wasm-smoke's test harness.
**/node_modules/
# The napi-rs addon `bun run build` writes for this machine, and the per-platform package
# directories `napi create-npm-dirs` writes (the Forge's pack-npm action runs it on a copy of
# typescript/ at release time); never committed.
typescript/*.node
typescript/npm/

# R. vendor.sh derives the wrapper crate's lock from rust/Cargo.lock, vendors the crates
# (the core among them, from this checkout) and stages the header and the corpus into these
# at release time, in CI and for the local loop; R CMD INSTALL leaves the objects and the
# library. All generated, never committed. r/.gitignore and typescript/.gitignore repeat
# their entries for their own trees.
r/src/rust/vendor/
r/src/rust/vendor.tar.xz
r/src/rust/Cargo.lock
r/src/.cargo/
r/src/include/
r/tests/testthat/corpus/
r/src/*.o
r/src/*.so
r/src/*.dll

# BenchmarkDotNet
# Writes output relative to the process's working directory when invoked via `dotnet run`
# rather than the project directory, so this can land almost anywhere in the tree — not just
# csharp/HyperTabular.Benchmarks/. Criterion's own output already lands under rust/target/,
# covered by the **/target/ rule above.
**/BenchmarkDotNet.Artifacts/

# IDE
.idea/
.vs/

# cargo-fuzz working state — the targets and Cargo.toml are tracked; the evolving corpus
# and any crash artifacts are machine-local (a reproducing crash gets minimized and
# committed as a regression test, not as a raw artifact).
rust/fuzz/corpus/
rust/fuzz/artifacts/
rust/fuzz/coverage/

# The corpus copy test-apple-mobile stages for the Go suite in the iOS simulator
# (go_ios_exec carries only the module's testdata), if made by hand.
go/testdata/corpus/

# CI artifacts downloaded to the repository root (`gh run download` with no --dir lands one
# folder per artifact here): native libraries, wheels, gems, packages and AOT reports from a
# ci.yml run. No binary is committed; these never belong in a commit. Anchored to the root
# so nothing tracked below it is touched.
/aot-report-*/
/native-*/
/nuget-org-*/
/php-ext-*/
/pypi-wheels-*/
/ruby-native-*/
/ruby-wasm-*/
/static-libs/
/swift-static/
/wasm-emscripten-staticlib/
/wasm-wasip1-module/

# The pinned HyperCast a board leg works with (the Forge's fetch-companions writes its source,
# its artifacts, the wiring's env and the job-local package folders here); never committed,
# and the release-mode guard fails a release whose checkout holds one.
.companions/

# What Windows attaches to a downloaded file, when the file is copied into WSL.
*:Zone.Identifier
# What Finder writes into any folder it opens.
.DS_Store

# A library's pins are its consumers' to make: HyperCast is resolved fresh from the range
# the manifests declare, by a release as by anyone depending on this package (a board run
# takes the pinned HyperCast run of .github/hyper.json instead, its manifests rewritten in the
# job only).
/Package.resolved
/swift/Package.resolved
/swift/StaticSmokeTest/Package.resolved

# The large benchmark inputs corpus/generate writes.
corpus/generate/out/

# cargo-fuzz's working state: the corpora rust/fuzz/seed.py writes and libFuzzer grows, and
# the inputs it saves when a target fails. A failing input worth keeping becomes a test.
rust/fuzz/corpus/
rust/fuzz/artifacts/
rust/fuzz/coverage/
